  "id": "charleroi",
  "scale": 1.25,
  "title": "Crossing the Sambre",
  "date": "15 June 1815",
  "blurb": "The Army of the North has crossed the frontier at dawn. Zieten's Prussian outposts hold the Sambre, a deep river in a steep valley, at the barricaded bridges of Charleroi and Châtelet, five kilometres apart. Beyond Charleroi the Fleurus road climbs through the long street of Gilly; behind a wooded brook Pirch II's brigade waits on the plateau of Soleilmont. Seize the bridges and Gilly before the Prussians can concentrate. A warm-up for the real work to come.",
  "hint": "The Sambre can only be crossed at the two bridges: Charleroi on your left, Châtelet on your right. Gilly's street is a death trap for cavalry. The Gilly brook can be waded, but the Prussian guns on the Soleilmont plateau look straight down on it: send a column round by the mill or from Châtelet.",
